I think it's good to learn how to manage a rampaging pet simply for
the fact that you are prepared for it when it is a neccessity (most
likely to stop it from killing an altar priest).  Knowing how to
corral your pet with a leash / magic whistle, and how they behave when
you leave them alone (do they open doors? is my minotaur going to hunt
down that tengu and eat its corpse?) aren't always a given.  I've
gotten in the habit of locking a pet in a one-room closet when I don't
want them killing NPCs or eating certain corpses.




